<header><p class="enc-kicker">Work / monument · text</p><h1 class="enc-title">Annals of Inisfallen</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Annals of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/inisfallen">Inisfallen</a> are a chronicle of medieval Irish history, preserved in a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/manuscript">manuscript</a> written largely in the late 11th century and continued by later hands into the 14th. They are associated with the monastery on Inisfallen in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lough-leane">Lough Leane</a> near <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/killarney">Killarney</a> and are a key source for the history of Munster. The manuscript is now in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bodleian-library">Bodleian Library</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/oxford">Oxford</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/annals-of-inisfallen.jpg" alt="Annals of Inisfallen" width="320" height="152" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: The manuscript is hundreds of years old, and was the work of numerous individuals. … · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Macc_Congail,_r%C3%AD_na_Rend.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
